   = \frac{4}{3}\pi (1.64\times10^{-6}\,\text{m})^{3}
   \approx 1.84\times10^{-17}\,\text{m}^{3}
\]

**2. Convert density to SI**  
\[
\rho = 0.851\ \frac{\text{g}}{\text{cm}^{3}}
      = 0.851\times10^{3}\,\frac{\text{kg}}{\text{m}^{3}}
      = 851\ \frac{\text{kg}}{\text{m}^{3}}
\]

**3. Mass of the drop**  

\[
m = \rho V \approx 851 \times 1.84\times10^{-17}
   \approx 1.57\times10^{-14}\ \text{kg}
\]

**4. Weight**  

\[
mg = (1.57\times10^{-14}\,\text{kg})(9.81\ \text{m/s}^2)
    \approx 1.54\times10^{-13}\ \text{N}
\]

**5. Electric field**  

\[
E = 1.92\times10^{5}\ \frac{\text{N}}{\text{C}}
\]

**6. Charge required**  

\[
q = \frac{mg}{E}
    = \frac{1.54\times10^{-13}\ \text{N}}{1.92\times10^{5}\ \text{N/C}}
    \approx 8.0\times10^{-19}\ \text{C}
\]

**7. Express in units of the elementary charge**  

\[
\frac{q}{e} = \frac{8.0\times10^{-19}\ \text{C}}{1.602\times10^{-19}\ \text{C}}
            \approx 5.0
\]

