The propagation (travel) time of a frame is simply the time it takes the radio‑frequency signal to cover the 10 m distance between the transmitter and the receiver.

\[
\text{Propagation speed}=2.8\times10^{8}\;\text{m/s}
\qquad
\text{Distance}=10\;\text{m}
\]

\[
\text{Propagation delay}= \frac{\text{Distance}}{\text{Speed}}
   = \frac{10\;\text{m}}{2.8\times10^{8}\;\text{m/s}}
   = \frac{1}{2.8}\times10^{-7}\;\text{s}
   \approx 3.57\times10^{-8}\;\text{s}
\]

